{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task. I need to implement a `solve(case)` function for task AGENT-TF-01.\n\nLooking at the fixture data, each case has:\n- `threshold`: a float\n- `calls`: a list of call objects, each with:\n  - `call_id`: string\n  - `loss_without_call`: float\n  - `loss_with_call`: float\n  - `prediction_tokens`: int\n  - `parseable`: bool\n\nThe output needs to be:\n- `accepted_call_ids`: list of strings\n- `diagnostics`: list of objects, each with:\n  - `accepted`: bool\n  - `call_id`: string\n  - `normalized_gain`: float\n\nNow I need to figure out what the logic is. Looking at the field names:\n- `loss_without_call` vs `loss_with_call` - the gain from the call is `loss_without_call - loss_with_call`\n- `prediction_tokens` - number of tokens\n- `parseable` - whether the output is parseable\n\nThe \"normalized gain\" likely normalizes the loss reduction by the number of prediction tokens:\n`normalized_gain = (loss_without_call - loss_with_call) / prediction_tokens`\n\nA call is \"accepted\" if:\n1. It is `parseable`\n2. The `normalized_gain \u003e= threshold`\n\nLet me verify with the fixture data.\n\nCase 000:\n- threshold: 0.05\n- call0: (1.94835097 - 0.38569502) / 5 = 1.56265595 / 5 = 0.31253119, parseable=true → should be accepted\n- call1: (1.06116273 - 0.68319969) / 4 = 0.37796304 / 4 = 0.09449076, parseable=true → should be accepted\n- call2: (1.21810502 - 0.47260371) / 6 = 0.74550131 / 6 = 0.12425022, parseable=true → should be accepted\n- call3: (1.05721833 - 0.29767903) / 5 = 0.7595393 / 5 = 0.1519079, parseable=true → should be accepted\n- call4: (1.06717367 - 0.85733566) / 5 = 0.20983801 / 5 = 0.04196760, parseable=true → 0.04196760 \u003c 0.05, NOT accepted\n- call5: (1.66191711 - 0.89798497) / 4 = 0.76393214 / 4 = 0.190983035, parseable=true → accepted\n\nSo accepted_call_ids for case 000 would be: call0, call1, call2, call3, call5\n\nCase 002 has call4 with parseable=false, so it should NOT be accepted regardless of normalized_gain.\n\nThe logic seems to be:\n- `normalized_gain = (loss_without_call - loss_with_call) / prediction_tokens`\n- `accepted = parseable AND normalized_gain \u003e= threshold`\n\nLet me code this up:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        normalized_gain = (loss_without - loss_with) / tokens\n        \n        accepted = parseable and normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain,\n            \"accepted\": accepted\n        })\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks right. Now I need to format it as a JSON response with the implementation key.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n\\n    for call in calls:\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n\\n        normalized_gain = (loss_without - loss_with) / tokens\\n\\n        accepted = parseable and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\\n\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain,\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted\\n        })\\n\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01tzsujt7Coi7oeiAjKNdUvI","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2146},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2146,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":71,"output_tokens":1224,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":979},"service_tier":"standard"}}